    "lawCode": "Add Title X §§62.01 - 62.08, Arts & Cul L; add §96-a, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Arts and Cultural Affairs Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3078\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the arts and cultural affairs law, in relation to\nindemnity for domestic exhibitions and artifacts; and to amend the\nstate finance law, in relation to creating the New York state arts and\nartifacts indemnity fund\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide authorization for the State to\nindemnify domestically held art and artifacts used for exhibition in\nNew York State, or those New York State collections loaned to\ninstitutions in other states.  Additionally, the bill will provide\nterrorism indemnity for exhibits both loaned and borrowed from within\nand outside the borders of New York.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 amends the Arts and Cultural Affairs Law to create the\nDomestic Indemnity Act including the following provisions:\n\n* Provides definition necessary to the program;\n* Authorizes the New York State Council on the Arts to enter into\nindemnity agreements for eligible items;\n* Defines those items eligible for indemnification;\n* Provides requirements for the application and approval process;\n* Sets coverage limits;\n* Sets deductible limits;\n* Provides that the premium for coverage shall be one-half of one\npercent of the total coverage sought, or $25,000 whichever is less;\n* Provides for a claims process; and,\n* Authorizes that the Legislature may make appropriations to pay\nclaims.\n\nSection 2 amends the State Finance Law to create the New York State\nArts and Artifacts Indemnity Fund. The fund shall consist of the\nrequired premiums. Twenty-five percent of the total fund balance may\nbe used for marketing and promotion purposes to advertise those\nexhibitions indemnified under this program.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date as April 1, next succeeding the\nenactment of this legislation.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrently, the federal Arts and Artifacts Indemnity Program only\ncovers those exhibitions either on loan from, or on loan to, foreign\ninstitutions. With the ever increasing cost of insurance premiums,\nmany museums, especially those smaller in size, have completely halted\nsecuring exhibitions, or participating in reciprocal loan programs.\nThis program is necessary to ensure that New York museums have the\nability to bring quality exhibitions to the public, which currently\nare not available due to insurance costs.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2005-06: A.6713-A - Passed Assembly\n2007-08: A.2491-A - Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThe legislation provides only an authorization to indemnify an\naggregate of $600,000,000. An appropriation is only made to cover\nclaims against the fund, after the deductible has been applied. In its\nthirty-one year long history, the federal program has only needed to\npay one claim totaling $134,000.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the first of April next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
